Package: winptp
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Abdulrahman <195754713+QuantumPixelNomad@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), python3-evdev, systemd
Recommends: kwin-wayland | kwin-x11, python3-pyside6.qtwidgets | python3-pyqt6, pkexec | policykit-1
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/QuantumPixelNomad/Linux-precision-touchpad-drivers
Description: Windows Precision Touchpad behaviour for KDE Plasma
 winptp is a userspace touchpad driver that reproduces how a Windows 10
 precision touchpad feels: pointer acceleration, taps, palm check,
 two-finger scrolling with inertia, pinch zoom and 3/4-finger gestures.
 It grabs the touchpad and drives KWin through virtual uinput devices.
